            <ArticleTitle>False-positive gray-scale ultrasonography for intra-abdominal abscesses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>810-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two patients had convincing mass lesions demonstrated with gray-scale echography and strongly supporting clinical evidence for intra-abdominal abscesses. Neither patient had a lesion at the time of surgery. Although modern echography is an accurate diagnostic method for intra-abdominal abscess, false-positive results can occur.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
